<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves to the banking system on Wednesday via overnight system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>The move was in line with the market's expectations.</p>
<p>By 1130 EST/1630 GMT, the time when the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
